Optional polish: add a "Claude Mode" entry to nocturne-ui's General settings.

The primary mode switch needs no source patch — `scripts/inject-firmware.js`
grafts `switch.js` into the built music UI, and holding preset 1 + preset 4 for
one second toggles between `/` and `/claude/`. This patch is for users who build
the UI from source anyway and want a visible menu entry too.

`usenocturne/nocturne-ui` is archived; since 4.1 the UI lives in the monorepo as
`packages/ui`, rewritten in TypeScript with MobX and react-router 7. Apply in a
checkout of https://github.com/usenocturne/nocturne:

    cd /path/to/nocturne
    git apply /path/to/claude-thing/patches/nocturne-ui-claude-mode.patch

Two edits in `packages/ui/src/components/settings/Settings.tsx`, both mirroring
the existing `factory-reset` action item:

1. In `settingsStructure.general.items` (immediately before the
   `id: "factory-reset"` entry, ~line 119):

```tsx
      {
        id: "claude-mode",
        title: "Claude Mode",
        type: "action",
        description:
          "Switch to the Claude Code session monitor. Hold preset 1 + preset 4 to come back.",
        action: "claudeMode",
      },
```

2. In `handleAction` (~line 365), a new case beside `factoryReset`:

```tsx
      case "claudeMode":
        try {
          window.localStorage.setItem("claude-mode", "1");
        } catch (e) {}
        window.location.assign("/claude/");
        break;
```

No other changes. `handleAction` is still an untyped `(action)` switch in 4.1,
so neither edit needs a type annotation, and the item objects are plain literals
in the same shape `factory-reset` uses.

`/claude/` is served from the same origin by the daemon's static server
(`crates/daemon/src/http/webapp.rs`, a `ServeDir` with root-index SPA fallback),
so this is a plain same-origin navigation; the Claude app's "Exit to Music"
action (and the preset chord) clears the `claude-mode` flag so the device boots
back into music mode.

NOTE: documented as an edit rather than a byte-exact diff because line numbers
in Settings.tsx shift between nocturne releases.
